@startuml
title Approved Session Authentication — Conceptual Flow
actor User
participant "Angular / browser" as UI
participant "Spring Security" as Security
participant "Spring Session JDBC" as Sessions
database PostgreSQL as DB
User -> UI : Supply credentials
UI -> Security : Login request with CSRF protection\n(endpoint and payload pending design)
Security -> DB : Verify provisioned account, BCrypt password\nand current enabled state
DB --> Security : Account verification result
alt Invalid credentials or disabled account
  Security --> UI : Generic authentication failure\n(contract pending design)
else Valid account
  Security -> Sessions : Establish server-side authenticated session
  Sessions -> DB : Persist shared session state
  Security --> UI : Opaque session identifier in HttpOnly cookie
  UI --> User : Show permitted role experience
end
UI -> Security : Same-origin /api/v1 request + session cookie\nCSRF protection for unsafe requests
Security -> Sessions : Resolve valid, non-idle-expired session
Sessions -> DB : Shared session lookup / activity state
Security -> DB : Validate current enabled state / authorization
Security --> UI : Authorized domain response or denied request
note over UI, Sessions
Production session cookie: HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax.
Server-enforced idle timeout: 30 minutes.
Backend enforces CUSTOMER / AGENT and ownership / assignment.
Unsafe requests, including login and logout, require CSRF.
Valid sessions may resume on reload; identifiers are not exposed to JavaScript.
Account provisioning is admin-controlled; no public registration.
Concrete endpoints, JSON, cookie names, CSRF transport,
schema and session lifecycle mechanics remain pending design.
end note
@enduml
